8</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1" align="char" char=" " charoff="50" valign="top">30.1 &#x000b1; 4.6</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tfn5"><label>&#x02020;</label><p>From Ciulli <italic>et al.</italic> (2006<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="bb6"> &#x025b6;</xref>). ITC titrations were performed in 0.1&#x02005;<italic>M</italic> HEPES&#x02013;HCl pH 7.7 at 300&#x02005;K.</p></fn><fn id="tfn6"><label>&#x02021;</label><p>ITC titrations were performed in 90&#x02005;m<italic>M</italic> sodium acetate, 5&#x02005;m<italic>M</italic> HEPES&#x02013;HCl pH 4.5 at 300&#x02005;K.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="table3" position="float"><label>Table 3</label><caption><title>Effect of point mutations on the thermodynamic parameters of nucleotide binding</title><p>&#x00394;&#x00394;<italic>G</italic>, &#x00394;&#x00394;<italic>H</italic> and &#x02212;<italic>T</italic>&#x00394;&#x00394;<italic>S</italic> are &#x00394;<italic>G</italic>                  <sub>mutant</sub> &#x02212; &#x00394;<italic>G</italic>                  <sub>WT</sub>, &#x00394;<italic>H</italic>                  <sub>mutant</sub> &#x02212; &#x00394;<italic>H</italic>                  <sub>WT</sub> and &#x02212;<italic>T</italic>(&#x00394;<italic>S</italic>                  <sub>mutant</sub> &#x02212; &#x00394;<italic>S</italic>                  <sub>WT</sub>), respectively. n.d., not determined.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead valign="bottom"><tr><th rowspan="1" colspan="1" align="left" valign="bottom">&#x000a0;</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="3" align="left" valign="bottom">R31A</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="3" align="left" valign="bottom">N98A</th></tr><tr><th rowspan="1" colspan="1" align="left" valign="bottom">&#x000a0;</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1" align="left" valign="bottom">&#x00394;&#x00394;<italic>G</italic> (kJ&#x02005;mol<sup>&#x02212;1</sup>)</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1" align="left" valign="bottom">&#x00394;&#x00394;<italic>H</italic> (k